    {
      "section_id": "osteotome_section_1",
      "section_title": "Osteotome",
      "section_order": 1,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_1",
          "subsection_title": "1. Introduction",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_1",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_01.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An osteotome is a chisel-like surgical instrument used to cut, divide, shape or remove bone. It usually has a strong metal shaft, a bevelled cutting edge and a proximal striking surface or handle, depending on its design."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It is commonly used in orthopaedic surgery, maxillofacial surgery, neurosurgery and selected reconstructive procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "OSCE identification statement:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is an osteotome, a chisel-like surgical instrument used to cut or shape bone. It has a bevelled cutting edge and a strong shaft, and may be operated manually or with a surgical mallet, depending on its design. It is used in procedures such as osteotomy, bone remodelling and selected joint or reconstructive operations.”",
                  "style": "quote"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "2. Classification of osteotomes",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_2",
              "group_title": "A. According to design",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Straight osteotome"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Has a straight shaft and cutting edge. Used for controlled bone division and shaping in appropriate surgical procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Curved osteotome"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Has a curved blade or shaft to facilitate access to selected anatomical contours."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Narrow osteotome"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Used where a narrow cutting edge is required for a more confined area."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "4. Wide osteotome"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Has a broader cutting edge for selected wider bone cuts or shaping tasks."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_3",
              "group_title": "B. According to clinical specialty",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Orthopaedic osteotome: used in bone division, remodelling and selected reconstructive procedures.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Dental or oral-surgical osteotome: used in selected procedures involving alveolar or other facial bones.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Neurosurgical osteotome: used in selected cranial bone procedures, depending on the operation and instrument design.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The exact names and designs vary between manufacturers and specialties."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "3. Labelled components",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_08.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "dvmcentral.com"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The main parts are:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Cutting edge"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The sharp distal edge that divides or shapes bone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Bevel"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The sloping surface that forms the cutting edge. Bevel orientation influences how the osteotome interacts with bone and the direction in which it tends to displace the cut."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Shaft or blade body"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The strong metal portion that transmits force from the handle or striking end to the cutting edge."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "4. Handle or grip"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allows the surgeon to hold and guide the instrument accurately."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "5. Striking end"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Present on mallet-driven designs. Receives controlled blows from a compatible surgical mallet."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Labelling tip: Some osteotomes have a handle designed for direct manual pressure, while others have a striking end. Describe only the components present on the instrument displayed."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "4. Principles of operation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_5",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An osteotome concentrates force along a narrow cutting edge to divide or separate bone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Manual pressure: some designs can be advanced by hand.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Mallet-assisted action: controlled blows drive the cutting edge into bone.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Controlled bone separation: the surgeon directs the instrument along a planned plane to achieve the required cut.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The cutting edge, blade orientation, applied force and bone characteristics influence the result."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Excessive force or an incorrectly directed osteotome may cause uncontrolled fracture propagation or damage adjacent structures."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "5. Indications and clinical uses",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_6",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_09.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Osteotomy"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Used to divide bone deliberately to correct deformity, alter alignment or change joint mechanics."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Bone remodelling"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Used to shape or remove selected portions of bone during reconstructive procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_10.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Maxillofacial surgery"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Used in selected jaw and facial bone procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/osteotome_11.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "4. Selected orthopaedic procedures"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "May be used for bone preparation, removal of bone fragments or selected reconstructive tasks, depending on the operation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Other uses depend on specialty and may include selected dental, spinal and neurosurgical procedures."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "6. Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Provides direct, controlled mechanical cutting of bone.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Does not require electricity or a powered drive.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Available in different widths and shapes for different surgical needs.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Can be useful in confined anatomical spaces.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Allows the surgeon to direct a cut along a planned plane.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Can be used with a mallet or manually, depending on design.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "7. Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_8",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Requires skill and controlled force.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Excessive force can cause uncontrolled fracture propagation.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "May injure adjacent nerves, vessels or soft tissues.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Cutting can be less rapid than powered techniques in some procedures.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A blunt or damaged edge can reduce cutting efficiency and compromise control.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Some designs require a compatible surgical mallet.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "8. Contraindications and precautions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "There is no universal contraindication to an osteotome; its use depends on the planned procedure and anatomical circumstances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "title": "Important precautions include:",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Confirm the intended bone cut and the anatomical structures at risk.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Inspect the cutting edge and shaft for damage.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Use a compatible mallet if the instrument is designed for mallet use.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Avoid uncontrolled or excessive force.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Protect adjacent soft tissues and neurovascular structures.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ensure the cutting edge is directed along the intended plane.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Follow appropriate sterilisation and instrument-handling procedures.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "9. Basic principles of safe use",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "For OSCE understanding; actual surgical use requires appropriate training and supervision."
                },
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Confirm the indication and planned cut.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "1."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Select an osteotome of suitable width, shape and bevel orientation.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "2."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Inspect the instrument for damage or a blunt cutting edge.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "3."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Expose the bone and protect adjacent structures.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "4."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Position the cutting edge along the intended plane.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "5."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Apply controlled manual pressure or use a compatible mallet, depending on the instrument.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "6."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Avoid excessive force and uncontrolled advancement.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "7."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Reassess the cut and surrounding structures.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "8."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Inspect the instrument after use and follow the appropriate reprocessing protocol.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "9."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "10. Complications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_11",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Explanation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Uncontrolled fracture propagation",
                      "The cut may extend beyond the intended plane."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Neurovascular injury",
                      "Adjacent nerves or vessels may be damaged."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Soft-tissue injury",
                      "The cutting edge or instrument movement may injure surrounding tissue."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Incomplete osteotomy",
                      "The intended bone division may not be fully achieved."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Excessive bone removal",
                      "Poor control may compromise the intended surgical result."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Bone splintering",
                      "May occur depending on the bone, technique and applied force."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Instrument damage",
                      "The cutting edge or shaft may become damaged under excessive loading."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Infection",
                      "Risk arises if appropriate aseptic technique is not maintained."
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "11. Differences between an osteotome, chisel and bone saw",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_12",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "This comparison is particularly important in instrument-identification OSCEs."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Feature",
                    "Osteotome",
                    "Chisel",
                    "Bone saw"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Appearance",
                      "Chisel-like bone-cutting instrument",
                      "Chisel-like cutting tool",
                      "Rigid toothed blade or flexible wire"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Cutting edge",
                      "Usually bevelled",
                      "Usually bevelled",
                      "Serrated teeth or cutting wire"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Primary action",
                      "Cuts or separates bone",
                      "Removes or shapes material; specialised surgical chisels may cut bone",
                      "Sawing movement divides bone"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Force",
                      "Manual pressure or mallet, depending on design",
                      "Usually manual or mallet-assisted",
                      "Manual reciprocal movement or powered movement"
                    ],
                    [
                      "Common use",
                      "Osteotomy and bone remodelling",
                      "Bone shaping or removal, depending on the type",
                      "Bone division in procedures such as amputation or joint replacement"
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Important qualification: The terms osteotome and chisel can overlap in surgical practice, and terminology varies by specialty and instrument design."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "osteotome_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "12. Common OSCE viva questions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "osteotome_group_13",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. Identify this instrument."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "This is an osteotome, a chisel-like surgical instrument used to cut or shape bone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. What are its main components?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Cutting edge, bevel, shaft, handle and, where applicable, a striking end."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. What is the principle of action?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It concentrates force at a cutting edge to divide or separate bone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. Name two clinical uses."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Osteotomy and bone remodelling."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. What is the difference between an osteotome and a Gigli saw?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An osteotome cuts bone with a bevelled edge using directed force, while a Gigli saw divides bone using a flexible serrated wire moved back and forth."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. Why is bevel orientation important?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It influences how the cutting edge engages bone and the direction in which the instrument may displace the cut."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. What are the major complications?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uncontrolled fracture propagation, soft-tissue injury, neurovascular injury and incomplete or inaccurate bone division."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. Why should excessive force be avoided?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It can cause loss of control, unintended fracture extension or injury to nearby structures."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
